> build-house-style · deepseek-v4.1-flash:1017-cloud
Static serving was already wired in the tree from step 01, so I tightened it and proved it end to end.

Changes:
- `internal/docker/application.go:55` — static container now uses `nginx:alpine-slim` (22 MB vs 96 MB).
- `internal/docker/application.go:59` — nginx config derives its health path and document root from `HealthCheckPath` / `staticContentTarget`, so the static container cannot drift from the app health-check contract.
- `integration/docker_test.go:86` — `TestStaticSiteDeployment` deploys a folder through the normal namespace/proxy path and asserts the proxied site, a nested file, and `/up` all serve over the proxy.

Verification (project lint command is `make lint`):
- `make test` → all packages ok
- `make lint` → `0 issues`
- `go test -run TestStaticSiteDeployment ./integration/` → PASS (real Docker, real kamal-proxy, folder bind mount, host routing, health check)
